<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I6a3a15feb6edd355d6ec252c36b6f7885b383099" commit="6ec4fb6dee19e588e222066949ff3af120193408" commit_message="UPSTREAM: cbfs/vboot: remove firmware component support  The Chrome OS verified boot path supported multiple CBFS instances in the boot media as well as stand-alone assets sitting in each vboot RW slot. Remove the support for the stand-alone assets and always use CBFS accesses as the way to retrieve data.  This is implemented by adding a cbfs_locator object which is queried for locating the current CBFS. Additionally, it is also signalled prior to when a program is about to be loaded by coreboot for the subsequent stage/payload. This provides the same opportunity as previous for vboot to hook in and perform its logic.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and ran on glados. CQ-DEPEND=CL:307121,CL:316960,CL:316961  Original-Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/12689 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Tested-by: Raptor Engineering Automated Test Stand &lt;noreply@raptorengineeringinc.com&gt; Original-Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Original-Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;stefan.reinauer@coreboot.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 6d720f38e06d14cc8a89635f66dc124dcd5ac150)  Change-Id: I6a3a15feb6edd355d6ec252c36b6f7885b383099 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316950 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="316950" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="14" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/50/316950/14" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3003afd029408fa984515d8ecc7c5c5309f53bdc" commit="ce0052058495bb541752f96148b7c228093f60e1" commit_message="Enable use of CBFS in RW sections  This switches boards over to use CBFS-formatted FW_MAIN_*, and gets rid of (EC|PD)_MAIN_[AB] in the process.  With several changes in other repositories (incl. upstream coreboot), this leads to a working image that jumps to RW and finds its EC firmware in CBFS, too.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=tot TEST=none CQ-DEPEND=CL:316950  Change-Id: I3003afd029408fa984515d8ecc7c5c5309f53bdc Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307121 Commit-Ready: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="5" gerrit_number="307121" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/21/307121/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="8"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ife5ec2c72e8263f83030a079367e7c52b016ef4a" commit="5d7c83c27ca23bbf151ab8dad30ef4accb1e80fd" commit_message="Handle multiple CBFS cleanly  libpayload already honors the lb_boot_media_params found in the coreboot tables. Therefore, no extra code is required to deal with multiple CBFS instances. Also, libpayload operates on absolute boot media offsets so there should be no translation required.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and ran on glados. CQ-DEPEND=CL:316950  Change-Id: Ife5ec2c72e8263f83030a079367e7c52b016ef4a Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316960 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="316960" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/60/316960/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8854dbbb061219d63498325280419bd489185b8e" commit="0291ae58680432ce1993a1da8a26b4d0955942bc" commit_message="Remove firmware components from vboot_handoff.  coreboot droppped firmware component support in the vboot_handoff struct when moving over to only support multiple CBFS instances. Therefore, update the vboot_handoff structure to match coreboot.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and ran on glados. CQ-DEPEND=CL:316950  Change-Id: I8854dbbb061219d63498325280419bd489185b8e Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316961 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="316961" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/61/316961/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I383fd6579280cf9cfe5a18c2851baf74cad004e9" commit="6b5a1487ecadd40793a70ffb81739b1b6dfa393d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: lib: remove assets infrastructure  Now that only CBFS access is supported for finding resources within the boot media the assets infrastructure can be removed. Remove it.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and ran on glados.  Original-Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/12690 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Original-Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;stefan.reinauer@coreboot.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 7e7a4df58075fdff4293d2203b035b970d21aeb8)  Change-Id: I383fd6579280cf9cfe5a18c2851baf74cad004e9 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316951 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="316951" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="14" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/51/316951/14" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I62ac675a34694a537af3dc48d5e53ddc2a3a8c5d" commit="88b49d3d6eac101d75236a248ad45a9a8a8e5b34" commit_message="CHROMIUM: sdhci: quirk for reset on tuning timeout  In some cases, data inhibit bits are not released on tuning timeout and will hang system.  Reset the controller after a tuning timeout to avoid this.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48472 TEST=force tuning timeouts  Change-Id: I62ac675a34694a537af3dc48d5e53ddc2a3a8c5d Signed-off-by: Christopher Freeman &lt;cfreeman@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317923 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317923" owner_email="cfreeman@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/23/317923/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ia4887f153d85a786e67e5c834bb4fab41579cf36" commit="f48ff227d2becd78541100ff84596e2a6cbd1268" commit_message="CHROMIUM: sdhci: tegra: use RESET_ON_TUNE_TIMEOUT quirk  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48472 TEST=force tuning timeouts  Change-Id: Ia4887f153d85a786e67e5c834bb4fab41579cf36 Signed-off-by: Christopher Freeman &lt;cfreeman@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317924 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317924" owner_email="cfreeman@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.